    "temperature": {
      "file": "bearing_housing_temperature.glb",
      "title": "Heat comes from the bearings; oil carries it to the housing",
      "description": "Friction in the bearings (thrust bearings more) heats the oil; the oil ring spreads oil and the finned housing rejects heat to air. Typical limits: bearing housing ≈ 80–85 °C or ≈ 40 °C above ambient (check the maker/API 610 guidance). Correct oil level matters: too low starves the bearings, too high churns and overheats. Bearing isolators keep water and dust out — contamination is the leading cause of bearing failure.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
